ttedName":"kris9685","Id":231919,"Name":"kris9685","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"e0be85102c60da5e61c1ef7fecf52ba8","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Beautiful! Great work on your STD!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1574740,"PostDate":1327796018,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Beautiful! Great work on your STD!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"Lovielyn@gmail.com","IpAddress":"99.242.209.218","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1326654721,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-249934.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Pappy","Id":249934,"Name":"Pappy","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"a8d9ff1b8444c0781ea9972d41d4ddfd","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Beautiful &amp;amp; very informative!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1574779,"PostDate":1327803126,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Beautiful & very informative!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"shanetaspinall@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"74.74.218.114","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1318883984,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-246807.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":99,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Palacebridex2","Id":246807,"Name":"Palacebridex2","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"01265599ae73389710e399332334b81c","RawContent":"i love how your STD passport turned out.  I&#039;m still trying to put mine together. We&#039;re doing the passport as our invitation :) [quote]\nOriginally Posted by [b]kris9685[\/b] \/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\n \n \n Hey Everyone! I cannot believe I completed my first DIY project for our wedding. We finished our passport save the dates &amp;amp; mailed them out last month. We have been so crazy I am just posting the info now. I used so many suggestions &amp;amp; sample ideas from this website I wanted to give back and share my experience for others to learn from. \n \n For starters I used the Ayleebits free template in Pages (on a Mac) to create the documents I also used Photoshop Elements to create the \"stamp\" images in the background of each page &amp;amp; the magnet. For the covers I ordered 3 custom stamps from www.simonstamp.com and used s silver ink pad I bought at Michael&#039;s. The Green covers are metallic card stock &amp;amp; the inner pages are sand colored heavyweight paper. I order all of our paper from www.paperandmore.com. We sewed the pages together using crochet thread I found at Walmart and it matched the color of the inside pages perfectly. \n \n Tools we used included paper cutters, corner rounders, a circle cutter, no-wrinkle glue, a laminater, business card sized magnets, removeable glue dots and a thick needle. \n \n In addition to the passports we made little magnets with a monogram and included the date &amp;amp; location on them. We used the removable glue dots to adhere the magnets temporarily to the back of the passports. \n \n Here are a few photos of the final product: \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500190\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n Front covers \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500192\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n Back sides with the magnets attached. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500194\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n We made 45 passports. I was so grateful that my 2 bridesmaids, aunt, mother, &amp;amp; fiance were all there to help me get these put together. My dad even helped with the magnets! \n \n We pretty much set up an assembly line to get these done. First cutting out the pages &amp;amp; rounding the corners. Then sewing the inner pages together, then glueing them to the outer page\/cover. Finally we stamped the fronts &amp;amp; let them sit over night. The ink took a while to dry so we needed to lay them out on a table. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500222\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n Here are the magnet&#039;s laid out. We attached them to the passports &amp;amp; stuffed the envelopes on another day. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500224\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n I made the envelope liners by taking the compas image I created &amp;amp; shrinking it down &amp;amp; multiplying it. I got this idea from someone on here &amp;amp; it came out perfect. \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500226\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n Front upclose \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500230\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n close up of the envelop liners \n \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500233\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n Here is a close up of the 1st page inside. I used the same idea with the smal replicated compases inside &amp;amp; the large one on top. The compass is the same as the one used for the stamp. I found an image I liked on Google &amp;amp; edited it to the way I liked it to look &amp;amp; added a J in the middle. We will probably carry this image through to our invitations &amp;amp; other pieces at the wedding. \n \n So because I used Pages to create these I didn&#039;t think many people would find the template useful. If you really want my template PM me and I&#039;ll send it to you. Instead I have converted the document to images so you can see the rest of the pages. Because of the way the template is set up the page numbers may seem strange, but when you put them together they are in the correct order. For printing- the 1st page (twice on one sheet of paper) I only printed them single sided as the would get glued down to the green covers. The other two pages were printed on the reverse of each other &amp;amp; I printed twice as many sheet as the 1st page. \n [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500235\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500240\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] [img]http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500242\/width\/1000\/height\/500[\/img] \n \n I hope this post can help someone else get ideas or answer some questions about creating these passports as I did when I started out. \n \n Feel free to ask me any questions you may have &amp;amp; let me know what you think!! \n[\/quote]","Attachments":[],"Id":1597091,"PostDate":1332266380,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> <br \/> i love how your STD passport turned out.\u00a0 I'm still trying to put mine together. We're doing the passport as our invitation <img src='http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/public\/style_emoticons\/default\/smile.png' class='bbc_emoticon' alt=':)' \/><\/p> <blockquote class=\"ipsBlockquote\">Originally Posted by <strong>kris9685<\/strong>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"View Post\" class=\"inlineimg\" src=\"\/img\/forum\/go_quote.gif\" \/><\/span><br \/> <br \/> <p> Hey Everyone! I cannot believe I completed my first DIY project for our wedding. We finished our passport save the dates & mailed them out last month. We have been so crazy I am just posting the info now. I used so many suggestions & sample ideas from this website I wanted to give back and share my experience for others to learn from.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> For starters I used the Ayleebits free template in Pages (on a Mac) to create the documents I also used Photoshop Elements to create the \"stamp\" images in the background of each page & the magnet. For the covers I ordered 3 custom stamps from www.simonstamp.com and used s silver ink pad I bought at Michael's. The Green covers are metallic card stock & the inner pages are sand colored heavyweight paper. I order all of our paper from www.paperandmore.com. We sewed the pages together using crochet thread I found at Walmart and it matched the color of the inside pages perfectly.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Tools we used included paper cutters, corner rounders, a circle cutter, no-wrinkle glue, a laminater, business card sized magnets, removeable glue dots and a thick needle.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> In addition to the passports we made little magnets with a monogram and included the date & location on them. We used the removable glue dots to adhere the magnets temporarily to the back of the passports.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Here are a few photos of the final product:<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Front Cover\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500190\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Front covers<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Back Sides with magents\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500192\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Back sides with the magnets attached.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"all on table\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500194\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> We made 45 passports. I was so grateful that my 2 bridesmaids, aunt, mother, & fiance were all there to help me get these put together. My dad even helped with the magnets!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> We pretty much set up an assembly line to get these done. First cutting out the pages & rounding the corners. Then sewing the inner pages together, then glueing them to the outer page\/cover. Finally we stamped the fronts & let them sit over night. The ink took a while to dry so we needed to lay them out on a table.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"magnets\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500222\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Here are the magnet's laid out. We attached them to the passports & stuffed the envelopes on another day.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"envelope liners\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500224\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> I made the envelope liners by taking the compas image I created & shrinking it down & multiplying it. I got this idea from someone on here & it came out perfect.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"front close\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500226\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Front upclose<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"close envelope\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500230\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> close up of the envelop liners<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"1st page\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500233\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> Here is a close up of the 1st page inside. I used the same idea with the smal replicated compases inside & the large one on top. The compass is the same as the one used for the stamp. I found an image I liked on Google & edited it to the way I liked it to look & added a J in the middle. We will probably carry this image through to our invitations & other pieces at the wedding.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> So because I used Pages to create these I didn't think many people would find the template useful. If you really want my template PM me and I'll send it to you. Instead I have converted the document to images so you can see the rest of the pages. Because of the way the template is set up the page numbers may seem strange, but when you put them together they are in the correct order. For printing- the 1st page (twice on one sheet of paper) I only printed them single sided as the would get glued down to the green covers. The other two pages were printed on the reverse of each other & I printed twice as many sheet as the 1st page.<\/p> <p> <span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Passport STD_v1.jpg\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500235\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Passport STD_v2.jpg\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500240\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span>\u00a0<span rel='lightbox'><img class='bbc_img' alt=\"Passport STD_v3.jpg\" src=\"http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/image\/id\/500242\/width\/1000\/height\/500\" \/><\/span><\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> I hope this post can help someone else get ideas or answer some questions about creating these passports as I did when I started out.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Feel free to ask me any questions you may have & let me know what you think!!<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <\/blockquote> <br \/> <br \/> <p> \u00a0<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"mzthan6@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1287426560,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-233303.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":180,"PhotoHeight":180,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"mzthan6","Id":233303,"Name":"mzthan6","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"44a7c73c48634d93daad4f72670e6351","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; WOW... you did an amazing job!!.. I ordered some samples of the passport invitations and I soo think I can turn to my crafty side and make my own.. Thanks for&amp;nbsp;the inspiration and your tips and pictures!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1597153,"PostDate":1332273118,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> WOW... you did an amazing job!!.. I ordered some samples of the passport invitations and I soo think I can turn to my crafty side and make my own.. Thanks for\u00a0the inspiration and your tips and pictures!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"britneyrasco@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":42,"GroupName":"Sr. Member","JoinDate":1329430672,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-251499.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"MissBubbles205","Id":251499,"Name":"MissBubbles205","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"7efb7a48cdb99586507e2f251028f99f","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; You did a fabulous job on these invites!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1598702,"PostDate":1332598894,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> You did a fabulous job on these invites!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"suzie_burnette@yahoo.com","IpAddress":"24.179.28.79","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1318262839,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-246479.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":300,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"Smitten","Id":246479,"Name":"Smitten","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"ca01e04138cbcb06dde289236d01b549","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; These look great. They are exactly what I am looking for. If you could share the template, that would be great.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thanks&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1603664,"PostDate":1333561265,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> These look great. They are exactly what I am looking for. If you could share the template, that would be great.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thanks<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"peterscakes@gmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1333561207,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-253606.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"peragano","Id":253606,"Name":"peragano","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"b263242e1f162ea27bd2ed2d14af621c","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Wow!!! Clearly a lot of love and maybe even a few tears went into making these.&amp;nbsp; They look like a professional did them! Congrats!!!&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1603669,"PostDate":1333561798,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Wow!!! Clearly a lot of love and maybe even a few tears went into making these.\u00a0 They look like a professional did them! Congrats!!!<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"<p>My Mayan Riviera Wedding Planning Journal (February 7, 2013)-\u00a0<a data-ipb='nomediaparse' href='http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/72926-tkuzmas-mayan-riviera-wedding-planning-journal-february-7-2013\/'>http:\/\/www.bestdestinationwedding.com\/topic\/72926-tkuzmas-mayan-riviera-wedding-planning-journal-february-7-2013\/<\/a>","Email":"tamara.om.kuzma@gmail.com","IpAddress":"70.74.167.106","GroupId":40,"GroupName":"Jr. Member","JoinDate":1327735209,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-250618.jpeg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":200,"PhotoHeight":127,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"tkuzma","Id":250618,"Name":"tkuzma","IsOnline":false}},{"Title":null,"ShowSignature":true,"ShowEmoticons":true,"IpAddress":"0.0.0.0","IsFirstPost":false,"IsQueued":false,"IsVisible":true,"IsDeleted":false,"CanEdit":false,"CanDelete":false,"CanLike":true,"TopicId":62588,"EditedBy":"","EditDate":0,"EditReason":"","DeleteDate":0,"TotalLikes":0,"IsLiked":false,"PostKey":"0441a21227683a2d2f71627b2cd1be69","RawContent":"&lt;p&gt; Wow, you really done an amazing job !&amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; I met my fiance in a plane. I am South african and he is Swiss. This would be great to use as a wedding invitation for us. Is it all possible that you can email me the templates? I would love to surprise him with this idea.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; &amp;nbsp;&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Thank you soooooooo much for your creative inspiration.&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; Dedr\u00a9&lt;\/p&gt; &lt;p&gt; desme1@hotmail.com&lt;\/p&gt;","Attachments":[],"Id":1616610,"PostDate":1336394172,"PostContent":"            <html>\r\n              <head>\r\n                <style type=\"\"text\/css\"\">\r\n                  body {\r\n                    font-size: 16px;\r\n                    font-family: Helvetica, Verdana;\r\n                  }\r\n                  img .bbc_img {\r\n                    width: 100%;\r\n                  }\r\n                <\/style>\r\n              <\/head>\r\n              <body>\r\n                <p> Wow, you really done an amazing job !\u00a0<\/p> <p> I met my fiance in a plane. I am South african and he is Swiss. This would be great to use as a wedding invitation for us. Is it all possible that you can email me the templates? I would love to surprise him with this idea.<\/p> <p> \u00a0<\/p> <p> Thank you soooooooo much for your creative inspiration.<\/p> <p> Dedr\u00a9<\/p> <p> desme1@hotmail.com<\/p>\r\n              <\/body>\r\n            <\/html>","Author":{"Signature":"","Email":"desme1@hotmail.com","IpAddress":"","GroupId":39,"GroupName":"Newbie","JoinDate":1336394025,"Photo":{"HasPhoto":true,"PhotoUrl":"http:\/\/bdw.stevewright.netdna-cdn.com\/cdn\/profile\/photo-255032.jpg?_r=0","PhotoWidth":150,"PhotoHeight":150,"PhotoType":"custom"},"FormattedName":"AfricanSwiss","Id":255032,"Name":"AfricanSwiss","IsOnline":false}}],"Pages":{"TotalItems":33,"TotalPages":4,"CurrentPage":10,"NextPage":20,"PreviousPage":0,"LastPage":30},"PushNotifications":[{"Key":"notifications","Value":0,"Type":"int"},{"Key":"messages","Value":1,"Type":"int"}]}
